Thus, the points $(a,b,c)$ which satisfy these inequalities form an infinite triangular pyramid.  We can split this into three cases.

**Case 1:** $a \ge b \ge c$

Then $c \le a$ and $c \le b,$ so the inequalities $a + c > b$ and $b + c > a$ are automatic.  Thus, we need only $a + b > c,$ which means $c$ ranges from 1 to $a + b - 1.$

**Case 2:** $a \ge c \ge b$

Then $b \le a$ and $b \le c,$ so the inequalities $a + b > c$ and $b + c > a$ are automatic.  Thus, we need only $a + c > b,$ which means $b$ ranges from 1 to $a + c - 1.$

**Case 3:** $b \ge a \ge c$

Then $c \le a$ and $c \le b,$ so the inequalities $a + c > b$ and $b + c > a$ are automatic.  Thus, we need only $a + b > c,$ which means $c$ ranges from 1 to $a + b - 1.$

Hence,
\begin{align*}
&\sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{b = 1}^\infty \frac{2^a}{3^b} \sum_{c = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{5^c} [a + b > c][a + c > b][b + c > a] \\
&= \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{b = 1}^{a} \frac{2^a}{3^b} \sum_{c = 1}^{a + b - 1} \frac{1}{5^c} + \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{c = 1}^a \frac{2^a}{5^c} \sum_{b = 1}^{a + c - 1} \frac{1}{3^b} + \sum_{b = 1}^\infty \sum_{a = 1}^b \frac{2^a}{3^b} \sum_{c = 1}^{a + b - 1} \frac{1}{5^c}.
\end{align*}These three sums are all equal, so the sum is equal to
\[3 \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{b = 1}^a \frac{2^a}{3^b} \sum_{c = 1}^{a + b - 1} \frac{1}{5^c}.\]We have that
\[\sum_{c = 1}^{a + b - 1} \frac{1}{5^c} = \frac{1}{5} \cdot \frac{1 - \left( \frac{1}{5} \right)^{a + b - 1}}{1 - \frac{1}{5}} = \frac{1}{4} \left( 1 - \frac{1}{5^{a + b - 1}} \right) = \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{4 \cdot 5^{a + b - 1}},\]so
\begin{align*}
3 \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{b = 1}^a \frac{2^a}{3^b} \sum_{c = 1}^{a + b - 1} \frac{1}{5^c} &= 3 \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{b = 1}^a \frac{2^a}{3^b} \left( \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{4 \cdot 5^{a + b - 1}} \right) \\
&= \frac{3}{4} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{b = 1}^a \frac{2^a}{3^b} - \frac{3}{4} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \sum_{b = 1}^a \frac{2^a}{3^b 5^{a + b - 1}} \\
&= \frac{3}{4} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \frac{2^a}{3} \cdot \frac{1 - \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^a}{1 - \frac{1}{3}} - \frac{3}{20} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \frac{2^a}{5^a} \sum_{b = 1}^a \frac{1}{3^b} \\
&= \frac{9}{8} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \frac{2^a}{3^a} \left( 3^a - 1 \right) - \frac{3}{20} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \frac{2^a}{5^a} \cdot \frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1 - \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^a}{1 - \frac{1}{3}} \\
&= \frac{9}{8} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \left( 1 - \frac{1}{3^a} \right) - \frac{9}{40} \sum_{a = 1}^\infty \frac{2^a}{5^a} \left( 1 - \frac{1}{3^a} \right) \\
&= \frac{9}{8} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{1}{3}} - \frac{\frac{1}{3}}{1 - \frac{1}{3}} \right) - \frac{9}{40} \left( \frac{\frac{2}{5}}{1 - \frac{2}{5}} - \frac{\frac{2}{15}}{1 - \frac{2}{15}} \right) \\
&= \frac{9}{8} \cdot \frac{2}{2} - \frac{9}{40} \cdot \frac{6}{13} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{108}{130}}.
\end{align*}
